### Account — Endpoints/AccountEndpoints.cs. Real HTTP requests instead of
### Blazor components because both touch the response before Blazor
### Server's circuit would start (sign-out, the OAuth challenge redirect —
### see dotnet-blazor:configure-auth). Neither is runnable as-is: both are
### form-bound POSTs, so ASP.NET Core's automatic antiforgery validation
### applies (same as Listings.http's photo upload) — get a session cookie +
### __RequestVerificationToken from a real browser session first.

@baseUrl = https://localhost:7105

### Sign out — normally posted by the app bar's AccountMenu form.
# @no-redirect
POST {{baseUrl}}/Account/Logout
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Cookie: .AspNetCore.Identity.Application={{authCookie}}

__RequestVerificationToken={{csrfToken}}&returnUrl=/

### Start an external-login challenge for one configured provider
### (google / microsoft / github — only providers with credentials set
### via user-secrets register at all, see docs/external-login.md). Redirects
### to the provider, so there's no useful JSON response to inspect here —
### this is really "click the button on /Account/Login", documented as an
### HTTP request for completeness.
# @no-redirect
POST {{baseUrl}}/Account/PerformExternalLogin
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Cookie: .AspNetCore.Identity.Application={{authCookie}}

__RequestVerificationToken={{csrfToken}}&provider=Google&returnUrl=/
